36,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"It seems our budget is tighter than we think; we're billed by area, not headcount, and every single power move costs us 6,200 yen per desk.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minato,,"I found out that the area by the printer is much noisier, and the physio says it takes days of small adjustments to get a workstation feeling right.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"The pilot floor's morning routine takes up to nine minutes per person, and those unplanned shuffles last year each caused two weeks of total chaos.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"The badge records show a huge gap in arrival times, and the staff survey makes it clear that daylight is the biggest complaint we've ignored.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I discovered that when project strands sat close, communication became much faster, and the new joiners learned the ropes just by overhearing our conversations.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@May, those unplanned shuffles sound like a significant drain on productivity, especially if we have to pay for every single power move.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Victoria, if it takes days to adjust a desk, moving often might be really tiring for our bodies too.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"Exactly. Between the time lost every morning and the chaos of shuffles, I'm worried that any ""flexible"" system will just eat our days alive.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, you're focusing on the time, but look at the badge records. A first-come, first-served system just means the early birds get the windows and the latecomers get the wall.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Shunichi, that's true, but the joiners' experience shows that sitting together helps us learn. Maybe the benefit of who we sit next to is worth more than the window?","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Daisuke, the benefit of communication is clear, but we must balance it against the cost. If we change layouts too often, the facilities fees and productivity loss will be unsustainable.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minato,,"@Daisuke, I agree that being close is nice, but if we move too much, I'm worried we'll never get our chairs and monitors adjusted to feel comfortable.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"@Minato, you're right. If we're constantly shifting, we're just spending our mornings fighting with monitor arms and plugging in cables instead of actually working.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Victoria, if we stick to a rigid plan to save money, we're just cementing the unfairness of who gets the window and who gets the noise. We can't just be ""rational"" about the budget.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I just don't want us to lose that natural way of helping each other. If we prioritize the window or the budget over who we sit next to, we might stop talking as much.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Victoria,,We need a solution that preserves our communication and budget without ignoring the physical discomforts Minato mentioned. Perhaps there is a middle ground between total rigidity and constant movement.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Minato,,"I think we should avoid anything that makes us move too often, because the noise and the chair settings are really important for focusing.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,"I'm with Minato. If we're losing nine minutes every morning just to set up, that's a huge waste of our limited gaps. We need something stable that doesn't create daily chaos.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"If we want stability and fairness, we can't just ignore the fact that some spots are objectively worse. A fixed plan only works if we're honest about who is sacrificing their comfort for the team.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"Maybe we can find a way to rotate so no one is stuck in the noisy spot forever, but not so often that it disrupts our work or the budget.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,,status,Victoria,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
57,3,,status,May,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
