61,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"Given the costs and the disruption May described, I believe Option A, Fixed Desks by Function, is the most rational choice to maintain our budget and productivity.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Minato,,"I'm worried about Option A because some of us would be stuck in the noisy area or with uncomfortable settings forever, so I'm leaning toward Option B.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,May,,"I agree with Minato. Option B, Rotating Blocks, seems like a better compromise; it avoids the daily chaos of Option C while ensuring no one is stuck in a bad spot indefinitely.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Victoria, Option A just formalizes the inequality. I'll vote for Option B, Rotating Blocks, because it's the only way to ensure the window and the noise are shared fairly.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,I see the value in Option B too; it lets us keep the communication benefits of sitting together while making sure everyone gets a turn at the window.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Daisuke, but consider the facilities cost. If we rotate blocks, do we risk more power moves? If Option B means shifting furniture, it could be a financial drain.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Victoria, if we just move our laptops and bags to a different block of existing desks, we wouldn't need to re-run the power cables every time.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,May,,"Exactly, Minato. As long as the desks are already there, we aren't paying for new wiring, just spending a little time moving our things occasionally rather than every single morning.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Victoria, the cost of a few moves a year is a small price to pay for a system where no one is permanently relegated to the wall or the printer noise.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,I agree. It seems like a fair way to balance the budget and the need for everyone to feel equal in the office.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"I see your points. If the rotation is infrequent enough to avoid significant productivity loss and doesn't require new wiring, Option B is a viable compromise. I will change my vote to Rotating Blocks.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Minato,,I'm glad we agree. I'll vote for Option B because it protects my need for comfort while being fair to everyone else.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,May,,I'll vote for Option B as well. It's the best way to avoid the daily stress of Free Address while still being fair about the environment.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,I'll vote for Option B. It's the most honest way to handle the layout without letting habit or luck decide who gets the short end of the stick.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I'll vote for Option B too. It feels like the best way to keep us connected as a team while making sure everyone is treated fairly.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Victoria,,"It is settled then. We all agree on Option B, Rotating Blocks, as the most balanced solution for our team.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Minato,,I'm happy we could find a way to make everyone feel comfortable and included.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,May,,I'm just relieved we aren't doing the daily shuffle. Let's make sure the rotation intervals are long enough to actually get some work done!,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"I'll agree to that. As long as the rotation is transparent and scheduled, we've successfully avoided the ""luck of the draw"" problem.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,I'm glad we could decide this together. I think we'll all feel much better knowing that the layout is fair for everyone.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
